<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n114331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, commonly in pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολάδες,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>bowels, guts,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.526
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				123
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antim.
				45
			</span></i>; made into strings for lyre, etc., <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.352.12
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>): in Com., also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολλάδες</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				246
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in sg.,
				<i>gut-cavity,</i> common to the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποχόνδριον</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαγών,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				493a21
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χόλ-ιξ,</span> Slav.
				<i>želad[ucaron]k[ucaron]</i> 'stomach';
			not cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χολή</span> as implied by
				<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>SD</u>
				2.9
			</span></i>.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
